# PocketWallet is non-custodial and client-side only — the setup flow needs NO
# server secrets. This file exists for the *next* build (balances / RPC), where
# you'll add a read-only RPC endpoint. Never put a private key or seed here.

# Public JSON-RPC endpoint used to read balances (read-only, safe to ship).
# The P0 wallet core is fully local and requires no environment variables.
# Future Bitcoin network providers must be replaceable and must never receive
# a mnemonic, seed, private key, decrypted wallet, or passcode.

# --- AUDD on Stellar (TESTNET PREVIEW, off by default) ---
# Only the exact value "testnet" turns it on. There is no mainnet option.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POCKETWALLET_STELLAR=testnet        # or mainnet-test (Ric's capped LIVE test: official AUDD only, A$300 cap, shared account only)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_MODE=self                    # testnet only: per-user self-custody path; default is the shared account (no per-user XLM)
# Optional clearly labelled stand-in asset for end-to-end testing, because AUDD
# testnet has no public faucet or liquidity. Must not use the code AUDD.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_TEST_ASSET=TAUD:G...ISSUER
# Optional testnet sponsor service (sponsor-worker/). When set, users need no XLM.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_SPONSOR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787   # Pocket Wallet AUDD service (ledger + optional sponsor); required for shared mode
